  abstract = {The complex scheme of atmospheric radical chain reactions is driven by a relatively small number of photodissociation processes. The most important ones in the troposphere are the formation of O(1D) by the photolysis of ozone (frequency J1), and the photolysis of NO2 (frequency J2). It is shown that uncertainties in J1 and J2 lead to large uncertainties in model-predicted species concentrations, particularly in OH levels. Methods of calculating/measuring J1 and J2 will be discussed.},
