  abstract = {The special incubus for the patient evoked by surgical interventions united with patient-own activities to overcome them and the influence on the course of the operation and the progress of recovery are explained. Variables of the individuality and the parameters of feeling have been recorded by psychodiagnostic methods in empirical studies at heart-patients and those needing in a general surgical treatment. This fact led to the proof of differentiated forms in the overcoming of operations-types by patients who differ from one another in the mastering of the event and the postoperative attitude. These types of accomplishment are the starting points for reflections on methods applyable in the psychological training for an operation according to personality feature.},
